Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["FindInfraParallel", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"7ff47a97-2b1b-4932-b98b-13d9278bb25c"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraParallel"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraParallel", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c415271-8bb1-4454-96ef-8dfe858c44a3"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives one parallel to ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] a geodesic through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " that stays at the distance ",
 StyleBox["d(p, line)", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " and cannot be prolonged at that distance \[LongDash] as a directed path \
graph.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"0ea168a4-63f9-4414-9891-2c532a8fcc1b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraParallel"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraParallel", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "246c335f-acaa-4ffa-9646-de9929179187"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a22ea99-3b3e-47e3-8aa3-8b47bd69e11f"],
 " of exactly ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " parallels or ",
 Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6674a79c-6b02-4f3d-8a77-79781cae7aff"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"UpTo", "[", "n", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b2db9f79-aa22-4da3-8078-d5d0633eaa84"],
 " gives up to ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43d26c97-b61a-4046-bd54-92b52593df84"],
 " gives the whole class as a pool of DAGs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"a42a6a3a-cb70-44bf-8331-e51cff8055db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " for the level set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], ":", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["v", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["l", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["e", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["l", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["e", "TI"]}], ")"}]}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79355c9c-4a6e-4e1e-8403-545719d01d19"],
 ". A parallel to ",
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is a geodesic ",
 StyleBox["s \[Ellipsis] p \[Ellipsis] e", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] so ",
 StyleBox["d(s, e) = d(s, p) + d(p, e)", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] with every vertex in ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 ", such that no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " in ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " prolongs it. This reads Euclid's fifth postulate intrinsically: constant \
distance is what a metric can say about parallelism without a notion of \
direction. Inextensibility is measured inside ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 ", not in ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", so a parallel need not be a line of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fb93bf84-09f1-4c5f-a828-1b1e7a88ae0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["line", "TI"],
 " is a vertex sequence, a walk graph, or a list of walk graphs, which \
spreads over its walks. Each parallel appears once, oriented so that ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " precedes ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 " in canonical order."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9d127113-e48b-45d8-878e-7aa2cd0b0582"],

Cell["\<\
On the square grid the classical picture survives: through a vertex of a \
parallel row there is exactly one parallel to a row, and it is the row. Off a \
line that bends, the level set bends with it, and a geodesic inside it soon \
has to leave \[LongDash] the parallels are then few and short. Below, through \
a vertex at distance 2 from a line through the centre, the square tiling has \
one parallel of 10 edges beside a line of 24, the irregular mesh two, of 4 \
and 5 edges, the hexagonal tiling a single edge. A vertex with no neighbour \
in its level set has no parallel at all: the class is empty, not the \
one-vertex walk.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"03ea728f-fef5-474c-8f87-3f731600b9df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraParallelQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraParallelQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "376e1a9a-acf2-4b7a-8290-4f162b59113a"],
 " asks a different question, and the two do not match. The predicate tests \
that two vertex sets are disjoint and at constant distance, and does not \
require either to be a geodesic. So it accepts pairs this function never \
returns \[LongDash] concentric shells, for instance, are parallel by that \
test \[LongDash] while every parallel returned here passes it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ba6032c7-796e-46a7-a17c-923f06b2151a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The class is carried by a ",
 StyleBox["pool",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": one geodesic DAG per admissible pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["e", "TI"],
 "), the ",
 StyleBox["s \[RightArrow] p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["p \[RightArrow] e", "TI"],
 " intervals cut down to ",
 StyleBox["L", "TI"],
 " and glued at ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ". Under the default ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa618aec-7ea9-4c9a-ae2f-62c9d93433ea"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85ffa903-b8d3-4230-a6d7-acbc453c67e2"],
 " returns the pool itself \[LongDash] a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f93a3c4e-ea43-4655-9d56-af10ff07020d"],
 " of DAGs, a single atom giving the one DAG. A bounded count streams \
parallels off the atoms as directed path graphs, and the count-less call is \
one parallel, deterministic."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"347f0d03-1f51-4165-8658-e4553a1c1484"],

